SUMMARY:Disposable Humanity – FREE
DESCRIPTION:Tuesday\, November 17\, 2026 • 7 PM • Steinman Hall A littl
 e-known chapter of Holocaust history. A story that demands to be remembere
 d. In Disposable Humanity\, the Mitchell family—esteemed Disability Stud
 ies scholars and filmmakers—examine the Nazi Aktion T4 program and its s
 ystematic murder of more than 300\,000 disabled people. Targeted as having
  a “life unworthy of living\,” these individuals became some of the Th
 ird Reich’s earliest victims of mass murder. Their deaths laid the groun
 dwork for the Holocaust that followed. Join us for this investigative docu
 mentary and an opportunity to explore its historical significance through 
 conversation with scholars\, advocates\, and community leaders. Admission:
